{
  "id": "ep017",
  "duration": 49.018,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.437,
      "text": "Voyager 2 launched two weeks before its twin, yet was named second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager 2 Launch - GPN-2003-000002.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_2_Launch_-_GPN-2003-000002.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.6,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.6,
          "end": 4.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.437,
      "end": 9.532,
      "text": "Most people assume the lower numbered spacecraft must have lifted off first.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager spacecraft (cropped).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_spacecraft_(cropped).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.433,
          "end": 8.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.0,
          "end": 9.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.532,
      "end": 17.552,
      "text": "In 1977, NASA utilized a rare planetary alignment occurring once every 176 years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "72413main ACD97-0036-3.jpg",
        "credit": "Nasa/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:72413main_ACD97-0036-3.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.533,
          "end": 12.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 12.567,
          "end": 17.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.552,
      "end": 23.072,
      "text": "Voyager 1 took a shorter and faster path to reach Jupiter and Saturn sooner.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Jupiter by voyager 1.jpg",
        "credit": "Voyager 1",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jupiter_by_voyager_1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.567,
          "end": 23.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.072,
      "end": 28.667,
      "text": "Meanwhile, Voyager 2 was sent on a longer journey toward the edge of the solar system.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager 2 on closest approach to Saturn.jpg",
        "credit": "Don Davis",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_2_on_closest_approach_to_Saturn.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.067,
          "end": 28.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.667,
      "end": 34.917,
      "text": "That detour made it the only spacecraft to ever visit the ice giants, Uranus and Neptune.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Uranus Voyager2 color calibrated.png",
        "credit": "Ardenau4",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uranus_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.667,
          "end": 34.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.917,
      "end": 41.967,
      "text": "It discovered rings and new moons before diving south and entering interstellar space in 2018.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Neptune Full.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neptune_Full.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.933,
          "end": 37.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 37.433,
          "end": 41.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.967,
      "end": 48.668,
      "text": "Reaching its destination second is why Voyager 2 launched two weeks before its twin, yet was named second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager 2 Launch - GPN-2003-000002.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_2_Launch_-_GPN-2003-000002.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.967,
          "end": 49.033,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
